faqItems:
  - question: "Can you design an enclosure from a sketch or explanation?"
    answer: "Yes, for suitable functional parts. Photos, a sketch and a description can start the discussion. We then establish the equipment dimensions, mounting points, clearances and access needed before agreeing the CAD and prototype work."
  - question: "Can you just print a model we already have?"
    answer: "Yes. Design work is only needed if the model or requirements call for it. We review the supplied files, discuss material, quantity and critical dimensions, then quote for printing. A sample is recommended before a larger order."
  - question: "Can you modify an existing model?"
    answer: "We assess the file and changes required. An editable CAD model or STEP file can help; substantial changes to an STL may require rebuilding geometry. We agree the approach before starting."
  - question: "Do you offer assembly and electronics integration?"
    answer: "These can be scoped into suitable projects. Previous work has included mechanical assembly, soldered wiring, illuminated buttons and custom microcontroller firmware. Tell us which hardware and software are already provided so the responsibilities and checks are clear."
  - question: "How accurate will the part be?"
    answer: "Critical dimensions and fits are discussed for the particular design, material and printer. We can tune the print process and make trial parts to assess them. There is no single tolerance promise covering every geometry; identify the features that matter before we quote."
  - question: "How are prototypes, changes and CAD files handled?"
    answer: "The quote sets out the expected development and print work. We discuss further changes if requirements move beyond that scope. Printed parts are the usual deliverable; STL, STEP or Fusion project exports can be agreed separately."
